    "type": "question",
    "label": "31",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\dfrac{x}{x+2}$ at $\\left(4,\\dfrac{2}{3}\\right)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x-18y+8=0$",
      "worked": "Let $u=x$ and $v=x+2$, so $u'=1$ and $v'=1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{1(x+2)-x(1)}{(x+2)^2}\\\\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=\\frac{2}{(x+2)^2}\\\\m&=\\frac{2}{(4+2)^2}\\\\m&=\\frac{2}{36}\\\\m&=\\frac{1}{18}\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}y-\\frac{2}{3}&=\\frac{1}{18}(x-4)\\\\18y-12&=x-4\\\\x-18y+8&=0\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
